cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use annplyr, please cite the software and, once published, the JOSS paper."
title: "annplyr: tidy AnnData wrangling in Python"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Manurung"
    given-names: "Mikhael"
    email: "mikhael.manurung@gmail.com"
    # [gap: ORCID] add `orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"` here.
    # [gap: affiliation] add `affiliation: "..."` here.
abstract: >-
  annplyr brings dplyr-style verbs to AnnData. Users filter, select,
  mutate, join, group and summarize cells and features through the
  adata.ap accessor. Every verb that returns AnnData keeps obs aligned
  with X, layers, raw, embeddings and pairwise matrices. Verbs that
  return tables give pandas DataFrames.
keywords:
  - AnnData
  - scverse
  - single-cell
  - tidy data
  - dplyr
  - data wrangling
  - pandas
repository-code: "https://github.com/mdmanurung/annplyr"
url: "https://mdmanurung.github.io/annplyr/"
license: "BSD-3-Clause"
version: "0.5.0"
date-released: "2026-09-27"
